## fix(inference): materialise rule triples that carry literal objects (#236)

Context: Business-rule inference (SWRL / Decision Table / Aggregate) computed and
reported its triples, but the materialisation step persisted only OWL-RL T-Box
schema triples to the `_inferred` Delta table. Rule consequents set datatype
attributes (literal objects, e.g. `greatWine "true"`, `tastingTier "Exceptionnel"`),
and the materialise filter required all three of subject/predicate/object to be
absolute HTTP(S) URIs — so every rule output was silently dropped. On a real build
the Inference report showed 6691 inferred but only 84 (schema) triples were
materialised; direct SQL on the `_inferred` table confirmed 100% schema predicates,
zero rule outputs.

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py — the materialise filter no
   longer requires the object to be a URI (RDF objects may be literals); it keeps
   the subject + predicate URI checks.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinInferredMaterialize.py — same relaxation
   in `uri_triples`.
3. tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_build_prepare.py,
   tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_background_tasks.py — updated the v0.9.0 tests
   that pinned the old drop; they now assert literal-object triples are kept and
   materialised (to both the Delta `_inferred` table and the graph). Safe because
   the store already routes literal objects (they land in `_data`/`_inferred` and
   the `_props` companion; adjacency traversal filters `object LIKE 'http%'` at
   query time, so a literal is never treated as an edge).

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinInferredMaterialize.py
- tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_build_prepare.py
- tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_twin_background_tasks.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" tests/units/dtwin tests/units/objects tests/units/architecture` -> 727 passed.

## fix(reasoning): make OWL axioms drive scalable graph reasoning (#237)

Context: OWL axioms declared in Expr. & Axioms never produced instance-level
inferences. `run_graph_reasoning` only expanded properties flagged via the
*legacy* property-characteristics panel (`_find_properties_by_characteristic`),
whose Transitive/Symmetric checkbox POSTs to removed `/ontology/constraints/*`
routes — so it always found nothing. The modern axiom path was never consulted,
and the owlrl T-Box pass runs on the ontology schema only (no instances, no scale).

Changes:
1. src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py — `run_graph_reasoning` now also
   reads `ontology["axioms"]`: a self `owl:propertyChainAxiom` (p ∘ p ⊑ p) marks
   p transitive and runs the existing scalable SQL `transitive_closure(p)`. New
   helpers `_find_transitive_from_axioms` and `_resolve_axiom_prop_uri` (resolve a
   property name/URI from an axiom to the data-namespace predicate URI).
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-axioms.js — require the result property
   for a `propertyChain` axiom (it was optional, so the chain's result could be
   saved empty and the axiom silently dropped at generation).
3. tests/units/ontology/test_reasoning_service.py — cover self-chain → transitive
   detection, the mixed-chain negative case, and `run_graph_reasoning` firing
   `transitive_closure` from a propertyChain axiom.

Not in this change (follow-up on #237): `owl:inverseOf` → SQL inverse expansion.
Its natural home (`GraphDBBackend`, beside `transitive_closure`/`symmetric_expand`)
is already over the 800-LOC class budget and the architecture ratchet forbids
growing it, so the inverse expander needs a budget-safe home first. General
`p ∘ q ⊑ r` chains likewise.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/reasoning/ReasoningService.py
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-axioms.js
- tests/units/ontology/test_reasoning_service.py

Tests: `uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" tests/units/dtwin tests/units/graphdb tests/units/ontology/test_reasoning_service.py tests/units/architecture` -> 1368 passed.
